# LotusDharma Architecture Boundaries

## Layer Separation Rules

### ❌ DON'T: Cross-layer imports
```typescript
// components/ ❌ DON'T import from lib/
import { apiClient } from '@/lib/api/client'; // WRONG

// app/ ❌ DON'T contain business logic
export default function Page() {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null); // WRONG - use TanStack Query
  // Complex business logic here... // WRONG
}
```

### ✅ DO: Respect boundaries
```typescript
// lib/ ✅ CAN import other lib modules
import { authStore } from '@/lib/stores/auth-store';

// components/ ✅ CAN import from lib/ (hooks, utils, stores)
import { useAuth } from '@/lib/hooks/use-auth';

// app/ ✅ CAN import components and lib utilities
import { MainLayout } from '@/components/layouts/main-layout';
import { getServerSession } from '@/lib/auth/utils';
```

## Import Hierarchy

```
app/ (routes only)
  ↓ imports from
components/ (UI only)
  ↓ imports from
lib/ (business logic only)
```

## File Organization Patterns

### Feature-based Components
```
components/features/
├── auth/           # Login, signup, profile
├── map/            # Map-related components
├── meditation/     # Meditation features
└── dashboard/      # Dashboard widgets
```

### API Client Structure
```
lib/api/
├── client.ts       # Base client with resilience
├── auth.ts         # Auth endpoints
├── data.ts         # Data endpoints
├── types/          # Generated TS types
└── utils/          # Retry, error handling
```

### State Management
- **Server State**: TanStack Query
- **Client State**: Zustand stores
- **Form State**: React Hook Form + Zod